Subject: VMS: let mch_breakcheck() and mch_delay() see the terminal mode

os_unix.c keeps the terminal mode in a static mch_cur_tmode, set only by its
own mch_settmode(), which VMS does not use (os_vms.c has its own). On VMS
mch_cur_tmode stayed TMODE_COOK, so mch_breakcheck() never checked for
typed keys: CTRL-C did not interrupt ":sleep", a long search, a slow ":g"
or a running script, and was only seen as a key when they had finished.
mch_delay() also never switched to TMODE_SLEEP.

On VMS use cur_tmode, which settmode() keeps for every platform and from
which it calls mch_settmode() when the mode changes.

--- a/src/os_unix.c
+++ b/src/os_unix.c
@@ -235,7 +235,15 @@
 #endif
 
 // Current terminal mode from mch_settmode().  Can differ from cur_tmode.
+#ifdef VMS
+// os_vms.c has its own mch_settmode(), which cannot keep the static
+// mch_cur_tmode up to date: use settmode()'s cur_tmode, which is the same.
+// Otherwise mch_breakcheck() never looks for typed keys, and CTRL-C cannot
+// interrupt ":sleep", a search or a running script.
+# define mch_cur_tmode cur_tmode
+#else
 static tmode_T mch_cur_tmode = TMODE_COOK;
+#endif
 
 #ifdef USE_XSMP
 typedef struct
